tops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed a deadlock in the trained network, but on the 9 dev episodes the edit scores the same as the original: 44.70 veh-h against 44.67. Any test gain depends on that deadlock happening in the test episodes.\n\n- **What I changed and why:** in one of the network's 6 recorded episodes it got stuck after traffic stopped arriving. It held phase 2 (EW_through) for about 1780 s, until the 30-minute drain cap, with nothing on its lanes while 3 cars waited elsewhere. That cost about 1.5 veh-h. I added a large penalty to any phase with no vehicles on its stop-line or upstream lanes. Four low-importance layer-1 units now detect \"this phase is empty\", and four layer-2 units turn that into a clean on/off signal that pushes the phase's logit down by 24. When no phase is empty, the penalty is the same for all phases, so the network decides as before.\n- **Parameters changed:** 252 of the allowed 371.\n- **Checks:** the edit makes the same decision as the original in 99.1% of normal recorded states; the ones that changed were near-ties. Whenever at least one phase has vehicles, it always picks one that does, including on 80,000 synthetic states. On the recorded stuck state it serves the waiting cars instead of staying on phase 2.\n- **Simulator calls:** 1 of 5. No vehicles were left at the cap in any episode, so the original probably didn't get stuck on dev either. I left 4 calls unused because I had no other change worth picking on 9 noisy episodes.\n- **Dev TTS:** 44.70 overall (low 34.7, nominal 44.8, high 54.6).\n- **Test predictions:** low 34.7, nominal 44.8, high 54.6. The expected gain is about 0–0.3 veh-h if the original gets stuck in some test episodes. If it never does, the near-tie decision changes could leave the result marginally worse (±0.2).\n\nEverything is in `work/`; open `NOTES.md` first.","ttft_ms":1424,"type":"result","duration_ms":837763,"uuid":"e1be9676-b167-4d01-a880-4e8ee0731060","ttft_stream_ms":863,"time_to_request_ms":49,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":8,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":4,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":1,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":75,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"deferred_tools_delta","slowest_producer_ms":3,"cpu_ms":11,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":3,"ambient_wait_ms":2,"render_ms":1,"producers":43,"token_counts":0},"tool_schema_build_detail":{"betas_ms":0,"waits_ms":1,"placement_ms":0,"render_ms":3,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"tools":14,"new_schemas":14},"message_normalization_detail":{"before_ms":0,"normalize_ms":1,"images_ms":0,"post_process_ms":0,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"messages":12,"wire_messages":2},"request_build_detail":{"records_ms":0,"system_ms":0,"headers_ms":1,"cache_break_record_ms":0,"plans_ms":1,"retry_setup_ms":0,"sent_build_ms":1,"record_attempt_ms":2,"other_ms":0,"sent_build_safety_context_ms":0,"sent_build_cache_breakpoints_ms":0,"sent_build_surrogate_scan_ms":0},"first_content_frame_ms":863,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-02T07:15:00.587Z"}
